   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "It happened to me, by accident",
     "texto": [
      "With **se + me / te / le / nos / os / les** you tell something that happened **by accident**.\n\n- **Se me olvidó** el nombre. (I cannot remember it.)\n- **Se me cayeron** las llaves. (They slipped out of my hands.)\n\nThe thing that falls, breaks or gets lost is the **subject**, and the verb agrees with it: one name → **olvidó**; several keys → **cayeron**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Who it happens to: me, te, le…",
     "texto": [
      "The pronoun says **who** it happened to:\n\n- to me → **se me** cayó\n- to you → **se te** cayó\n- to him, her, you (formal) → **se le** cayó\n- to us → **se nos** cayó\n- to you (plural, Spain) → **se os** cayó\n- to them, you (plural) → **se les** cayó\n\nTo be clear, add **a + person**: **A Lucía** se le rompió el móvil. The verb still agrees with the thing that breaks."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
